sseau, Burke, Mill, Marx, and Nietzsche.\u00a0 In each case, we will attend to the particular crises these theorists addressed in their work\u2014such as the European wars of religion, the English Civil War, colonialism, the French Revolution, and industrial capitalism\u2014as well as the broader philosophical and political issues they continue to pose to us now.\u00a0 Our approach will be both historical and conceptual, in other words, with the hopes of providing students with a nuanced but clear understanding of political theory as a distinctive form of political inquiry.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "Although not a prerequisite, GOVT 1615 can be taken in sequence with  GOVT 3626.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "(PT)", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 351398, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "1817", "titleShort": "Making Sense of World Politics", "titleLong": "Making Sense of World Politics", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1209, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "09:30AM", "timeEnd": "01:00PM", "startDt": "06/25/2018", "endDt": "07/13/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "vpg1", "firstName": "Chip", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Gagnon"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Lincoln Hall 107", "bldgDescr": "Lincoln Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "LNC107", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Summer Session class 