tral place in world affairs from the turn of the twentieth century down to the present. Beginning with the end of the Ottoman Empire and European colonization and domination of the entire region following WWI, we will study the emergence of Arab, Turkish, Persian nationalisms and Zionism, social and religious reform, the discovery of oil and its strategic importance in world political economy, the role of the region in the Cold War between the US and the Soviet Union, the conflict between Israel, the Palestinians and the Arab states, the political use of Islam and 9/11/01 and its aftermath, the Arab uprisings of the last few years and the civil wars that followed, and the American sponsored nuclear agreement with Iran. Assigned readings and film viewing will be supplemented with translated primary sources for use in class and section meeting discussions.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(HA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 359630, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3071", "titleShort": "Intro to Public Policy", "titleLong": "Introduction to Public Policy", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1211, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "06:30PM", "timeEnd": "09:15PM", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/27/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "ds90", "firstName": "David", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Silbey"}], "pattern": "T", "facilityDescr": "Wolpe Center 118", "bldgDescr": "Wolpe Center", "facilityDescrshort": "WLP118", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}, {"classMtgNbr": 2, "timeStart": "09:00AM", "timeEnd": "11:45AM", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/27/2018", "instructors": [], "pattern": "R", "facilityDescr": "Wolpe Center 118", "bldgDescr": "Wolpe Center", "facilityDescrshort": "WLP118", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Taught in Washington, DC. This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=659"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "DC", "locationDescr": "Washington, DC", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/27/2018", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "08/07/2018", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Public policy is shaped by many forces. This course will enhance your ability to understand those forces and the policies that they produce. It will provide you with tools for thinking about, assessing, and evaluating those policies. And it will introduce you to the substantive core of several major issues in America today. The course will have three segments. In the first, we will examine the relevant institutions, interests, and ideologies which operate in the policy arena and the debates about the impact of these forces which engage students of the policy process. In the second, we will consider two different lenses through which we might peer to evaluate policies. In the third, we will discuss the main lines of debate in contemporary American politics concerning four substantive issues: crime and punishment, education, the economy and foreign trade, and foreign policy. The course will meet four days a week for one hour. Based on assigned readings, the class sessions will mix lectures, discussions, group activities, and guest speakers.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 357918, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3128", "titleShort": "America's Changing Faces", "titleLong": "America's Changing Faces", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1213, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "07:00PM", "timeEnd": "08:55PM", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/27/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "klb297", "firstName": "Katie", "middleName": "Crosley", "lastName": "Beem"}], "pattern": "R", "facilityDescr": "Wolpe Center 118", "bldgDescr": "Wolpe Center", "facilityDescrshort": "WLP118", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Taught in Washington, DC. This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1749"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "DC", "locationDescr": "Washington, DC", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/27/2018", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1, "unitsMaximum": 1, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3128", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "08/07/2018", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "As new generations of leaders emerge in America's political, economic, educational, and cultural institutions (for good and ill), a national conversation about what constitutes leadership has continued.\u00a0 This course will examine the idea of that leadership at the national, community, and personal levels to understand the interactions between different kinds of leadership, how it connects to ideas of citizenship, communal and political engagement, and how generations shift their ideas of leadership.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "(AM)", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 351417, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3141", "titleShort": "Prisons", "titleLong": "Prisons", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1215, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "05/30/2018", "endDt": "06/22/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "mfk2", "firstName": "Mary", "middleName": "Fainsod", "lastName": "Katzenstein"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1883"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/30/2018", "endDt": "06/22/2018", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "DW", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL WWW", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning - WWW", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3141", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "3WK", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "06/22/2018", "sessionLong": "Three Week Summer", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "The United States stands alone among Western, industrialized countries with its persistent, high rates of incarceration, long sentences, and continued use of the death penalty. This \"American exceptionalism\" -- the turn to mass incarceration -- has been fostered by the use of sharply-delineated categories that define vast numbers of people as outlaws and others as law-abiding. These categories that are based on ideas of personal responsibility and\u00a0assumptions about race are modified somewhat by a liberal commitment to human rights.\u00a0\u00a0 Our purpose in this course is to understand how such ideas have taken root and to locate the consequences of these ideas for policy and practice.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, winter, summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 359631, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3150", "titleShort": "The Amer Legal System", "titleLong": "The American Legal System", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1222, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "09:00AM", "timeEnd": "12:00PM", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/13/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "ces78", "firstName": "Charles", "middleName": "Evan", "lastName": "Stewart"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Taught in NYC. This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1747"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "CENYC", "locationDescr": "Continuing Ed in NYC", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "07/13/2018", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "08/07/2018", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "This course offers a comprehensive introduction to the American legal system, its roots in natural and common law, the purposes/values it serves (e.g., resolution of private grievances; punishment of offenses against the polity and individuals; preservation, development, and limitation of individual and group rights; and facilitation of commerce and private agreements), and the roles of the judiciary, legislature, and private parties. The course is taught using the Socratic method employed at most US law schools and introduces students to fundamental concepts and techniques used by attorneys and courts in analyzing cases, interpreting statutes, and determining disputes. As in law school, students are expected to read assigned materials before each class meeting and to participate actively in class discussions. For additional information, see the Summer Session website.\n\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(CA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 351429, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3323", "titleShort": "Modern European Politics", "titleLong": "Modern European Politics", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1226, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:00AM", "timeEnd": "06:00PM", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "06/22/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 4, "netid": "jdh293", "firstName": "Jason", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Hecht"}, {"instrAssignSeq": 3, "netid": "keb11", "firstName": "K.E.", "middleName": "", "lastName": "von Wittelsbach"}, {"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "crw12", "firstName": "Christopher", "middleName": "Robert", "lastName": "Way"}], "pattern": "MTWRFS", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Taught in Italy. This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1935"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "TURIN", "locationDescr": "Turin, Italy", "startDt": "06/04/2018", "endDt": "06/22/2018", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "SOC", "catalogNbr": "3310", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2018", "sessionEndDt": "08/07/2018", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Introduction to politics and political systems in Western Europe.\u00a0 Starts with a brief history of the consolidation of West European democracies before and after World War II. Discusses core theoretical concepts guiding the comparative analysis of political systems. The main part of the course consists of a discussion of the political cultures, parties, electoral systems, and current problems confronting the political systems of various countries focusing on Italy which is treated in depth. The course concludes with an analysis of the European Union (EU) as political system.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2699, "crseId": 368788, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3887", "titleShort": "Int'l Human Rights Theo & Prac", "titleLong": "Int'l Human Rights in Theory & Practice", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1545, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "09:30AM", "timeEnd": "12:00PM", "startDt": "06/25/2018", "endDt": "07/13/2018", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "eb456", "firstName": "Elizabeth", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Brundige"}], "pattern": "MTWRF", "facilityDescr": "Myron Taylor Hall 277",